<title>UK: SBC adds $100 million to three-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>SBC adds $100 million to three-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC (Jersey) has increased to $400 million from $300 million the size of its 5.75 percent December 1999 bond, lead manager SBC Warburg said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The new paper was reoffered at 99.95.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Friday, November 29.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	 *$400 MLN  COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    09.DEC.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.1375  PAY DATE    09.DEC.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.96     SPREAD	FLAT</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JER</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  SWITZ     TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.1875    SELL CONC  1.1875    PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 5.875 PCT U.S. TREASURY NOTE DUE 15.NOV.99</p>
<p> NOTES     *INCLUDES $300 MLN LAUNCHED AT 100.9975/99.81 REOFFER</p>
